1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,810
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:06,710
Watch your step.

5
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:07,910
(Episode 65)

6
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:20,860
Seong Woo...

7
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:24,160
was a truly good friend.

8
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:29,170
If only that hadn't happened...

9
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,470
If only he'd kept
his nose out of it.

10
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,140
Is that why...

11
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:42,250
you killed him?

12
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:47,320
No...

13
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:49,850
I had...

14
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:55,030
I had no choice. No...

15
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:06,810
Darn it.

16
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:15,350
No...

17
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:17,950
I had...

18
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,850
I had no choice. No...

19
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:27,030
From here on out,
So Yeon is practically family to me.

20
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:31,830
I'm just looking out for my family,
so don't feel burdened by it.

21
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,040
After killing my dad,

22
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:44,980
you were only afraid
of getting caught.

23
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,150
Then you planned
to marry me off to Hae Ra.

24
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,280
Kang Young Hoon.

25
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,390
Was that the reason you accepted me?

26
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:03,800
Seok Jin, why are you
coming out of there?

27
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:05,930
Are you still drinking with Dad?

28
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:08,670
The CEO is asleep in his room.

29
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:12,700
Then, what were you doing
in the study?

30
00:02:14,270 --> 00:02:15,970
I just wanted to take a look around.

31
00:02:17,710 --> 00:02:18,710
I'll get going.

32
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:32,360
How much did you drink
with Chief Cha yesterday?

33
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,960
Are you still feeling that rough?

34
00:02:35,330 --> 00:02:37,160
Maybe because it's been so long
since I drank that much,

35
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:38,860
I just can't shake this hangover.

36
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,430
You said you drank makgeolli, right?

37
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,630
- Yes.
- No wonder it's worse.

38
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:44,800
I made hangover soup...

39
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:48,340
specifically for you,
so at least have some of the broth.

40
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:49,670
Will do.

41
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,080
Are you done already?

42
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,220
Why not finish your meal
before leaving?

43
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,790
No, I feel uncomfortable.

44
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,560
Aren't you feeling well either?

45
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,300
No, it's not that.
I'm going to head out.

46
00:03:24,810 --> 00:03:25,810
You...

47
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,280
What on earth are you hiding?

48
00:03:29,110 --> 00:03:31,950
What are you hiding that you'd go
so far as to pretend to be my mom?

49
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,370
Mom, you're here.

50
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:52,840
Gosh, what brings you here
this early in the morning?

51
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:56,510
The second I woke up,
I really wanted to see you.

52
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:58,280
Did I surprise you?

53
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:01,410
Not at all. I'm glad you came.
Have a seat.

54
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,920
How's assisting the Chairman?
Isn't it exhausting?

55
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,260
No, not at all.

56
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,830
I'm learning so much from her.

57
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,760
Learning? Like what?

58
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,660
From the overall operations
of the foundation...

59
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:21,970
to the specific plans going forward,

60
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:24,740
the Chairman has been teaching me
every little detail.

61
00:04:25,470 --> 00:04:27,070
Oh, really?

62
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,710
At this rate,

63
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,710
I'll get the hang
of the foundation's work in no time.

64
00:04:35,410 --> 00:04:38,520
What good is any of that going to do
for someone like you?

65
00:04:39,050 --> 00:04:40,790
How dare you set your sights
on that?

66
00:04:42,150 --> 00:04:45,020
So I'm really looking forward
to what's ahead.

67
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,330
It's nice to see your passion.

68
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:51,060
And if there's ever anything
the Chairman needs help with,

69
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:52,630
give me a little heads-up.

70
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,970
That way, I can be ready on my end.

71
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:57,440
I'd rather not tell you, Mom.

72
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,740
You already have a lot of work
as it is.

73
00:05:03,010 --> 00:05:04,580
I don't want to burden you
unnecessarily.

74
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:06,810
No matter how tired I am,

75
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:09,380
it's my daughter's work,
so of course I should help.

76
00:05:09,850 --> 00:05:12,180
Just say the word.
I'll do anything for you.

77
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:17,090
Eun Seol, I'm your mom.

78
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:20,960
I just want to give you
everything I can.

79
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:25,130
If you wanted to do so much for me,
why didn't you look for me sooner?

80
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:27,670
What?

81
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,470
Just saying.

82
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:35,510
I'm just so sad
we didn't reunite sooner.

83
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:41,180
The past doesn't matter.
What matters is what's ahead of us.

84
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,820
Now we get to be together like this
for the rest of our lives.

85
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,920
Well, now that I've seen you,

86
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:49,290
I should get going.

87
00:05:51,090 --> 00:05:52,390
Sure, go about your day.

88
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,860
Look at you pushing your luck.

89
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:03,530
The way she pushes people's buttons
while flashing a smile.

90
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,340
She's just like her mom.

91
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:08,140
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

92
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:14,210
Hae Ra's dad filled in
that settlement thing for me.

93
00:06:24,790 --> 00:06:27,760
What is this, a ticking time bomb?

94
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:32,130
Come in.

95
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:37,470
Did you call for me?

96
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,570
Director Joo, listen.

97
00:06:41,770 --> 00:06:42,770
How has...

98
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:45,010
So Yeon been doing lately?

99
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:49,250
Everything looked normal
at her routine checkup.

100
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,520
Why don't you pay her a visit,
Director Joo?

101
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:55,690
She's been seeming
anxious again lately.

102
00:06:56,190 --> 00:06:58,390
Even during dinner the other day,

103
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:02,260
she overreacted to nothing.

104
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:03,560
Did she?

105
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:05,730
I'll go see her after work.

106
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:07,930
Thank you, Director Joo.

107
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:11,300
Check on her
and report back right away.

108
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,810
Yes, sir.

109
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:17,640
Hey.

110
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,410
My dad must have had
a great time yesterday.

111
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:22,350
He got pretty drunk.

112
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:24,950
I had a great time too.

113
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:28,590
That was the first time I'd had
a real heart-to-heart with the CEO.

114
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:30,520
What did you two talk about
that was so fun?

115
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:31,620
Fill me in too.

116
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,560
I think having makgeolli
for the first time in a while...

117
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:36,260
brought back old memories for him.

118
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,500
He missed my dad a lot.

119
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:42,700
He seemed to have regrets too.

120
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,570
Though regretting it now
is pointless.

121
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,070
Really?

122
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:50,170
Maybe I should treat him
to makgeolli more often.

123
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:52,110
I'm planning on having
more moments like that.

124
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:54,310
The CEO enjoyed it,
and more importantly,

125
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,010
I found it genuinely interesting.

126
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:58,920
And I gained a lot from it.

127
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,990
All right, I'll let him know.

128
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:08,260
I heard you were having a rough time
right up until this morning.

129
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:10,130
Tell me about it.

130
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:16,130
How do you look
totally fine already?

131
00:08:16,170 --> 00:08:17,940
Is it because you're still young?

132
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,840
Yesterday was really tough
for me too.

133
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:23,240
Of course.

134
00:08:23,370 --> 00:08:26,840
After drinking that much,
there's no way you'd be fine, right?

135
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,180
By the way,

136
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:31,280
I was pretty drunk yesterday.

137
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,120
Did I do anything out of line?

138
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:37,120
No, not at all.

139
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,560
Really?

140
00:08:40,090 --> 00:08:41,160
That's a relief.

141
00:08:42,090 --> 00:08:43,460
Yesterday, you reminded me...

142
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:46,260
so much of my late father.

143
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:49,570
Really? I reminded you of Seong Woo?

144
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:53,470
It might take some time,

145
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,870
but I want to be a son-in-law
who feels like a real son to you.

146
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:59,010
I'll do my very best going forward.

147
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,910
Sounds good to me.

148
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:06,080
Something feels off about this.

149
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,860
We're just here to inform you today.

150
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,960
Eun Guk.

151
00:09:14,230 --> 00:09:17,090
You know what?
I'm proud of you, son.

152
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:20,460
How long will you keep walking
on eggshells around your grandma?

153
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:23,940
Since you've made up your mind,
you might as well get it over with.

154
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,770
What did you come here for then?

155
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:29,110
Why don't you just go ahead
and have the wedding without me?

156
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,540
Grandmother,

157
00:09:32,010 --> 00:09:34,310
I'm not asking
for your blessing right away.

158
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:37,850
Just keep me around
and see what I'm made of.

159
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:41,620
Even after all that, if you
still think I'm not right for him,

160
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:43,790
I'll walk away.

161
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:45,860
Mi Rae.

162
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:47,960
My situation is different
from yours, Eun Guk.

163
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:51,730
If everyone isn't on board
with me opening my heart again,

164
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:54,030
I'd rather not even start.

165
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,940
What's this?

166
00:10:05,710 --> 00:10:06,710
It's salt.

167
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,850
What, salt?

168
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:12,050
Am I kimchi cabbage?
Are you trying to salt me?

169
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:15,650
Father warned me
you'd go on a hunger strike,

170
00:10:15,690 --> 00:10:17,320
so I came prepared.

171
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:21,030
Even if you're refusing to eat,
your body still needs sodium.

172
00:10:24,730 --> 00:10:27,400
I picked up some roasted bamboo salt
just for you.

173
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:30,700
Once you start fasting,

174
00:10:30,770 --> 00:10:32,770
please take 1 granule every 4 hours.

175
00:10:33,070 --> 00:10:35,240
Make sure you don't skip it.

176
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:45,320
Hae Ra's dad scares me to death.

177
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:48,820
Really?

178
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:50,820
Yes.

179
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,460
I said the wrong thing yesterday,

180
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:55,760
and he...

181
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,330
looked at me like this.

182
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,470
You must've gotten
quite a scare, So Yeon.

183
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,200
By the way,

184
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:08,670
what did you say that was so wrong?

185
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,010
Well, you see...

186
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:19,220
It's all right.
You can tell me everything.

187
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:23,020
After all, I'm one
of your guardians now, So Yeon.

188
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:26,620
I can't.

189
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,690
He said if I told anyone,

190
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:31,260
Mr. Seok Jin would be in danger.

191
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:34,200
I'm never telling you.

192
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:39,140
Goodness.

193
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,270
Director Joo, what brings you here?

194
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:44,980
You're off work early today,
Chief Cha.

195
00:11:45,310 --> 00:11:46,310
Right.

196
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,110
What brings you to my house?

197
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,710
Well,

198
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:52,420
I bought some cookies
that So Yeon might like.

199
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,850
I had a meeting nearby, you see.

200
00:11:55,450 --> 00:11:56,950
I see.

201
00:11:57,990 --> 00:11:59,020
Then...

202
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,130
I'll get going now.

203
00:12:02,330 --> 00:12:04,360
Thank you for watching out
for my mom.

204
00:12:04,430 --> 00:12:07,430
Oh, please.
There's nothing to thank me for.

205
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:12,000
See you next time, So Yeon.

206
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:15,170
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

207
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,640
Take care.

208
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:24,950
Mom,

209
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:26,820
what were you doing
with Director Joo?

210
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:29,790
We didn't do anything.

211
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:32,420
Nothing happened.

212
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:36,360
I just said that Hae Ra's dad
was a little scary.

213
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:39,460
And? What else did you say, Mom?

214
00:12:39,730 --> 00:12:42,170
That I said
the wrong thing yesterday...

215
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:43,970
and he got super scary.

216
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:46,770
And then Director Joo asked,

217
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:50,640
"What did you say
that was so wrong?"

218
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:52,980
Don't tell me
you told her everything.

219
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,610
What's wrong, Mr. Seok Jin?

220
00:12:56,610 --> 00:12:58,620
I didn't tell her anything.

221
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:01,720
You can't be put in danger,

222
00:13:02,050 --> 00:13:04,390
so I kept my mouth tightly shut.

223
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:06,060
Like this.

224
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,800
Director Joo will accompany her.

225
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,630
From here on out, So Yeon...

226
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,730
is practically family to me.

227
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:20,870
I'm just looking out for my family,
so don't feel burdened by it.

228
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:24,310
(Cheongun Gaon
Senior Care Residence)

229
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,750
It's too dangerous
for Mom to stay here.

230
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,950
Still, I can't put her
in a care facility.

231
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:50,570
If Director Joo isn't
my birth mother,

232
00:13:52,070 --> 00:13:55,070
why did Manager Na
even leave these behind?

233
00:13:59,610 --> 00:14:02,010
Then what do these items
actually mean?

234
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,150
(Cheongma)

235
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:13,720
You mean Director Joo
is preparing her next move?

236
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:14,960
Yes.

237
00:14:15,390 --> 00:14:17,530
She tried to bring you down
with smear articles,

238
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,700
but that fell through.

239
00:14:18,930 --> 00:14:22,200
So she's likely targeting loopholes
in the scholarship program.

240
00:14:23,870 --> 00:14:24,970
That makes sense.

241
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,870
Then, how should we prepare?

242
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,010
First off, don't take anything
Director Joo says in meetings...

243
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:32,280
at face value.

244
00:14:32,710 --> 00:14:34,410
If it's hard to decide right away,

245
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:37,780
it's better to put it on hold
and take things slow.

246
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,820
All right.

247
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:42,350
Going over everything carefully
before we act is our safest bet.

248
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,360
(Cheongun Gaon
Senior Care Residence)

249
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,660
Chief.

250
00:14:54,570 --> 00:14:56,870
Have you been looking into
nursing homes?

251
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:02,540
My mom needs somewhere
to stay for a bit,

252
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:03,970
so I'm just exploring options.

253
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:07,340
I don't have
much of a choice right now.

254
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:10,710
Is something going on with your mom?

255
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,520
It's not that
something happened to her,

256
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:18,360
but just in case,
I want to put her somewhere safe.

257
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,590
Finding a place that works
is harder than I thought.

258
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:25,260
Moments like this
make being an only child...

259
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:28,100
with no one to lean on
feel pretty lonely.

260
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:33,200
Then what about having her stay
at my place?

261
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,440
Your place?

262
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:40,580
I don't know what's going on,

263
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:43,350
but if she just needs
a safe place to stay,

264
00:15:43,410 --> 00:15:45,480
I think I can help.

265
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:48,490
I heard the Chairman stayed...

266
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,850
at your place recently.

267
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:53,560
Won't we be imposing on your family?

268
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,030
My dad and grandmother
will understand.

269
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,000
And above all,

270
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:00,660
your mother will feel comfortable
if I'm around.

271
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:02,670
That's true.

272
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:05,670
She has been missing you
a lot lately.

273
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:09,470
Don't bother looking for a facility.

274
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:12,510
I'll look after her for a few days.

275
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,180
Are you sure it's okay?

276
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,780
What? A guest?

277
00:16:23,150 --> 00:16:25,060
Of course, we don't mind at all.

278
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,560
I see.

279
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,330
Let her know she can relax
and make herself right at home.

280
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,860
Sure. See you later.

281
00:16:33,230 --> 00:16:36,600
What is it?
Are we getting another freeloader?

282
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,400
Yes, I think so.

283
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,900
Apparently, it's someone
Eun Seol is very grateful to.

284
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:46,210
Does she seriously think our house
is some kind of guesthouse?

285
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:48,180
Do you have a problem with it?

286
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,010
No, I love it.

287
00:16:50,950 --> 00:16:53,320
I wonder what's in it for us
this time.

288
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,950
Mom, seriously.
All you care about is money.

289
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,460
If it's someone
who's been good to Eun Seol,

290
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:01,990
of course we'll take care of them,
money aside.

291
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:05,430
Fine, your mother is a materialistic woman
who only cares about money.

292
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,700
Happy now?

293
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:08,470
Hold on.

294
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:11,940
- Should we tidy up the place?
- Yes.

295
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,010
Clean it properly.
I'll take care of the bathroom.

296
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,580
Nice lady!

297
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,250
How have you been?

298
00:17:29,690 --> 00:17:31,120
Not good.

299
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:34,430
I missed you so much, nice lady.

300
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:38,430
Wait, did you cut your hair?
It's pretty.

301
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:41,600
You look even prettier,
like a princess.

302
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:44,900
You're the real princess here,
nice lady.

303
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,470
Mom, are you all packed?

304
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:51,680
Yes, but are we going somewhere?

305
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:55,180
Are we going on a trip together?

306
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,510
No.

307
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:59,120
You just need somewhere safe
to stay for a bit.

308
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:00,550
Then...

309
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:04,560
are you sending me
somewhere far away all by myself?

310
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:06,820
Away from you, Mr. Seok Jin?

311
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,160
No.

312
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:11,060
You'll be staying with me
for a while.

313
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:14,730
Really? I love it!

314
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:18,600
I wanted to draw with you,
nice lady.

315
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,600
Are you that happy, Mom?

316
00:18:21,370 --> 00:18:22,470
Yes.

317
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:26,410
Then does this mean I can sleep...

318
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,080
side by side with you as well?

319
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:31,250
Yes, of course.

320
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:35,550
I'm so happy to see you.

321
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:37,520
You look so pretty.

322
00:18:44,730 --> 00:18:46,730
Hello, Grandmother, Father.

323
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:48,700
Yes, hello. Come on in.

324
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,640
Make yourself at home.

325
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:54,040
- Thank you.
- Wait.

326
00:18:54,270 --> 00:18:56,540
Excuse me, hello.

327
00:18:56,710 --> 00:19:00,080
I am Park So Yeon.

328
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,080
I am...

329
00:19:02,650 --> 00:19:05,020
fifty-eight years old.

330
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:09,150
My son is Cha Seok Jin,

331
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,620
and he is 29.

332
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,720
I hope we get along.

333
00:19:13,790 --> 00:19:15,990
Right.
It must have been quite a trip.

334
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:18,200
Eun Seol, help put her bags away.

335
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:19,830
Right, her bags.

336
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
You know,

337
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:25,340
this new guest seems a bit off.

338
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,140
Or is it just me?

339
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:28,840
Stop. Keep your voice down.

340
00:19:40,150 --> 00:19:43,220
But that meticulousness was
his downfall.

341
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,290
That's...

342
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:48,530
what made things
spiral out of control.

343
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:49,660
I know he must have...

344
00:19:50,090 --> 00:19:52,730
tucked it away somewhere safe,

345
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:57,230
but I just can't find it.

346
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:01,840
Dad must've left
some records behind.

347
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:05,240
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

348
00:20:05,310 --> 00:20:06,380
Come in.

349
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,180
Hey, you're here. Have a seat.

350
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:15,820
Is something wrong?

351
00:20:17,490 --> 00:20:19,320
I'm just frustrated, that's all.

352
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:23,560
Why? What's going on?

353
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,470
Why were you...

354
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:32,100
standing so close to Ko Eun Seol
in the hallway the other day?

355
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,400
Ko Eun Seol?

356
00:20:36,010 --> 00:20:39,340
We just ran into each other
by chance.

357
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,450
What did you two talk about?

358
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:45,320
Since she'll be helping your mom
from now on,

359
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:48,720
I told her to come to me first
if anything like this happens again.

360
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,090
That's only proper.

361
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:54,460
Dad, it's no use.

362
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,560
Mom's really close to her.

363
00:20:56,730 --> 00:20:58,300
She's close with your mom?

364
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:01,530
When Mom left the house,
she wasn't staying at a hotel.

365
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:02,670
Then where?

366
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:04,370
She was staying
at Ko Eun Seol's place.

367
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,400
At Ko Eun Seol's place?

368
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:09,210
The two of them schemed there
and published that article.

369
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,370
Is that so?

370
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:12,540
Ko Eun Seol is something else.

371
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,250
How did she even win Mom over?

372
00:21:15,780 --> 00:21:18,550
She's a sneaky one, I'm telling you.

373
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:23,290
So that's what happened.

374
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,830
Wait.
What brings you here at this hour?

375
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:37,270
I thought we could
grab lunch together.

376
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,300
Didn't you say you had lunch
with Director Oh Tae Seop?

377
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,840
I canceled it.

378
00:21:42,170 --> 00:21:46,110
That's too bad.
I was going to eat with Eun Seol.

379
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:50,010
When Mom left the house,
she wasn't staying at a hotel.

380
00:21:50,610 --> 00:21:52,350
She was staying
at Ko Eun Seol's place.

381
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:56,050
Even better. I'll just tag along.

382
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,560
You too?

383
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:00,060
Yes.

384
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:03,760
It might make Eun Seol
uncomfortable.

385
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,600
Why would it?

386
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:07,700
How often does
an entry-level employee...

387
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:09,330
get to have lunch with the CEO?

388
00:22:09,330 --> 00:22:11,270
She'll probably be thrilled.

389
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:14,040
Fine, join us if you want.

390
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:15,440
Let's go.

391
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:29,190
I actually wanted to treat you
to a meal anyway, Ms. Ko.

392
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:35,790
All for her sake, you went
straight to my wife's ex-manager.

393
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:39,460
I really appreciate that.
It couldn't have been easy.

394
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:43,630
Not at all.
I only did what anyone would do.

395
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:48,310
Even family hesitates
to step up like that.

396
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:49,970
Thank you so much.

397
00:22:51,910 --> 00:22:53,540
However...

398
00:22:54,510 --> 00:22:57,680
As I mentioned before,
if anything like this happens again,

399
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,580
let me know first.

400
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,020
That way, I can do right by her...

401
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:06,590
both as her husband
and as the company's owner.

402
00:23:07,090 --> 00:23:08,190
Understood?

403
00:23:09,860 --> 00:23:12,130
Yes, sir. I will.

404
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,870
Your food's ready.

405
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:16,270
Right, thank you.

406
00:23:20,770 --> 00:23:21,970
Thank you.

407
00:23:22,470 --> 00:23:23,470
Oh, dear.

408
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:27,410
Look at how much we have in common.

409
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,610
Sharing an egg allergy
is rare enough.

410
00:23:33,050 --> 00:23:35,420
I was worried
since it can be genetic,

411
00:23:35,490 --> 00:23:37,450
but Hae Ra turned out
completely fine.

412
00:23:38,190 --> 00:23:39,320
What a relief.

413
00:23:40,190 --> 00:23:41,360
Please, go ahead and eat.

414
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:44,630
Right.

415
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:52,140
So...

416
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:54,640
Hae Ra's birthday is...

417
00:23:55,810 --> 00:23:57,770
September 11, right?

418
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,180
Yes.

419
00:23:59,780 --> 00:24:00,840
Oh, right.

420
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:04,180
Eun Seol, isn't your birthday
September 11, too?

421
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:07,420
What a coincidence.

422
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:10,520
Then the hospital she was born in...

423
00:24:10,690 --> 00:24:13,490
There's an old place
called Taeseon Hospital.

424
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:16,030
A friend of mine was working there.

425
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:21,460
Then...

426
00:24:23,730 --> 00:24:26,500
What's Hae Ra's blood type?

427
00:24:26,570 --> 00:24:27,770
She's type A.

428
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:31,710
I see you've been pretty curious
about Hae Ra.

429
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:35,580
It's a relief
she didn't take after me.

430
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:38,280
True.

431
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:43,390
He has type A negative blood,
which is pretty rare.

432
00:24:56,130 --> 00:24:58,070
(Patient is adopted.
Caution for blood transfusion)

433
00:24:58,130 --> 00:25:01,810
Blood type mismatch with family.

434
00:25:12,150 --> 00:25:15,250
Why aren't you eating?
Don't you like it?

435
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:19,920
No, it's not that.

436
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:23,090
I'm suddenly not feeling too well.

437
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:25,600
I'm really sorry, excuse me.

438
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:37,770
The CEO has type A negative blood.

439
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,310
No way.

440
00:25:44,510 --> 00:25:46,680
There you are, Eun Seol.

441
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:48,990
Did you have lunch?

442
00:25:50,020 --> 00:25:51,020
Yes.

443
00:25:51,390 --> 00:25:53,820
What? That hurts my feelings.

444
00:25:54,060 --> 00:25:55,790
Since I helped you
with the interview last time,

445
00:25:55,930 --> 00:25:57,390
I thought you'd treat me.

446
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:00,230
I'll buy you lunch next time.

447
00:26:00,860 --> 00:26:03,830
Wait, is something wrong?

448
00:26:04,570 --> 00:26:07,100
No. I'm just going to get going.

449
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,360
What are you looking at?

450
00:26:28,730 --> 00:26:29,730
It's nothing.

451
00:26:30,530 --> 00:26:31,860
So annoying.

452
00:26:32,230 --> 00:26:34,100
Stop spacing out
and do your job properly.

453
00:26:34,160 --> 00:26:35,770
Completely useless.

454
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:51,480
Why do you keep
getting involved with him?

455
00:26:51,550 --> 00:26:53,120
I told you to cut him off.

456
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:55,720
Who got involved with someone
like that in the first place?

457
00:26:58,390 --> 00:26:59,490
Come in.

458
00:27:02,990 --> 00:27:04,090
Here's the list of candidates...

459
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,530
for the scholarship program
you requested.

460
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:06,600
Right.

461
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:11,000
How is Ms. Kang doing lately?

462
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:14,340
Does she seem to be settling into
the scholarship program work?

463
00:27:15,470 --> 00:27:16,540
No.

464
00:27:17,370 --> 00:27:21,640
To be completely honest,
she seems pretty out of place.

465
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:24,680
In what way?

466
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:26,380
She frequently misses meetings...

467
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:29,320
and barely glances at the reports.

468
00:27:29,690 --> 00:27:31,350
Then, refusing to lose
to Ko Eun Seol,

469
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:33,260
she lets her pride take over.

470
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:38,560
She seems to handle her work
far too emotionally.

471
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:39,700
Is that so?

472
00:27:41,430 --> 00:27:42,500
That's why I told you...

473
00:27:43,030 --> 00:27:46,070
to look out for Ms. Kang
and help her out from up close.

474
00:27:46,970 --> 00:27:48,740
She's just a little clumsy at work,

475
00:27:48,940 --> 00:27:50,210
but her heart's in the right place.

476
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:52,180
Right, of course.

477
00:27:52,380 --> 00:27:55,150
She's not malicious by nature
like Ko Eun Seol.

478
00:27:57,210 --> 00:27:58,350
All right.

479
00:27:58,980 --> 00:28:01,850
Anyway, give this to Hae Ra.

480
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:04,920
It's the new program
we'll roll out...

481
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,620
once we halt
the correctional scholarship program.

482
00:28:06,760 --> 00:28:09,460
You're halting
the scholarship program?

483
00:28:09,530 --> 00:28:11,860
How long do you expect me
to watch Kim Jung Sun show off?

484
00:28:12,130 --> 00:28:15,470
We need to shut that program down
and shift the spotlight onto us.

485
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:17,970
Understood.

486
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,870
Just make sure to give her that
right away.

487
00:28:29,510 --> 00:28:31,280
Seriously,

488
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:33,980
where's her head at these days?

489
00:28:44,290 --> 00:28:46,500
How long do you expect me
to watch Kim Jung Sun show off?

490
00:28:46,860 --> 00:28:50,030
We need to shut that program down
and shift the spotlight onto us.

491
00:28:55,540 --> 00:28:57,870
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

492
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:20,600
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

493
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:33,440
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation
Young Artist Development Proposal)

494
00:29:37,910 --> 00:29:38,920
What's this?

495
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:42,850
Why is a new scholarship program
being prepared right now?

496
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:55,300
Team Leader Kang!

497
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,000
What now?

498
00:30:02,170 --> 00:30:03,410
You, follow me.

499
00:30:09,610 --> 00:30:11,850
What are those two plotting now?

500
00:30:27,030 --> 00:30:29,300
What on earth
have you been up to lately?

501
00:30:30,130 --> 00:30:31,370
I told you, didn't I?

502
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:34,070
Now is a more critical time
than ever.

503
00:30:34,770 --> 00:30:37,810
You need to deliver results
with the scholarship program.

504
00:30:38,580 --> 00:30:40,110
I know, I get it.

505
00:30:40,810 --> 00:30:42,480
My head feels like
it's going to explode too.

506
00:30:43,210 --> 00:30:44,450
That guy's pushing me from behind,

507
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:46,080
and you're coming at me
from the front.

508
00:30:46,150 --> 00:30:47,720
I'm going crazy here too!

509
00:30:48,020 --> 00:30:51,450
Have you still been meeting up
with him?

510
00:30:52,620 --> 00:30:54,060
Didn't I tell you to stay away?

511
00:30:56,530 --> 00:30:58,260
Now you're playing the mother card?

512
00:31:00,230 --> 00:31:02,270
Does giving birth make you a mom?

513
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:06,370
Then you shouldn't have switched
Eun Seol and me in the first place.

514
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:10,410
Why? Are you scared
I'll be thrown out of Cheongma?

515
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:12,880
Kang Hae Ra.

516
00:31:13,880 --> 00:31:14,940
Don't worry.

517
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:17,580
I'll never let anyone take my place.

518
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:21,650
But I'm the one who decides
how this goes.

519
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:28,520
Kang Hae Ra!

520
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:12,000
(A Trap Called Desire)

521
00:32:12,270 --> 00:32:14,600
Director Joo, did you look into
a new place to move into?

522
00:32:14,670 --> 00:32:17,470
- Attorney Baek.
- Taking a break from treatment?

523
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:19,510
Is there really no other reason?

524
00:32:19,510 --> 00:32:21,910
Chief Cha seems different somehow.

525
00:32:22,150 --> 00:32:24,250
The owner of Cheongma?
You've lost your mind.

526
00:32:24,450 --> 00:32:26,280
Wherever I go, it's Ko Eun Seol this,
Ko Eun Seol that.

527
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:28,620
Do you really have to compare me
to her too, Director Joo?

528
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:30,850
Don't worry about a thing, Princess.

529
00:32:30,950 --> 00:32:32,460
I'll take care of everything.

530
